---

## Quick Starter Code (React + Vite + Tailwind)

```bash
npm create vite@latest my-ecom -- --template react-ts
cd my-ecom
npm i -D tailwindcss postcss autoprefixer
npx tailwindcss init -p
```

Add Tailwind directives to `index.css`:

```css
@tailwind base;
@tailwind components;
@tailwind utilities;
```

Now you’re ready to start building components, pages, and services as outlined above.

---

### Final Thought

Building a frontend for an e‑commerce site is a marathon, not a sprint. Start small—get a “Hello World” page working, then iterate: add product listing, cart, checkout, authentication, admin panel, etc. Keep the code modular, test often, and let the community’s tooling (Vite, Tailwind, React Testing Library) do the heavy lifting.

Happy coding! 🚀
